                        ],
                        "examples": []
                    },
                    {
                        "sense_id": "12f03cbe-3ac0-3b2d-8c14-12049dfe8b6f",
                        "entry_id": "f910de3c-6330-39c0-8274-126853e5af84",
                        "glosses": [
                            "A heavy defeat, drubbing, or beating; used particularly in sports and political contexts."
                        ],
                        "tags": [
                            "US",
                            "countable",
                            "informal",
                            "uncountable"
                        ],
                        "examples": [
                            {
                                "example_id": "a1b45801-8ad0-44c0-8652-f9a5e0b5c0d6",
                                "sense_id": "12f03cbe-3ac0-3b2d-8c14-12049dfe8b6f",
                                "text": "The News baseball team defeated the Press-Guardian outfit, 8 to 4, in a recent game, which squares accounts for the shellacking the News received a year ago."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8eec9ca9-a0ea-4859-8deb-931e42460f32",
                                "sense_id": "12f03cbe-3ac0-3b2d-8c14-12049dfe8b6f",
                                "text": "Mourned Candidate La Guardia: \"What a shellacking they gave me!\""
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "8924631c-db80-492b-a4b0-a26a4f684270",
                                "sense_id": "12f03cbe-3ac0-3b2d-8c14-12049dfe8b6f",
                                "text": "Our baseball team got off to an indifferent start at the beginning of the season, but […] \"Steve\" Newman gave Gonzalo another shellacking that he won't forget for some time."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5be994c1-44fe-47a2-8d55-425934c2d6bd",
                                "sense_id": "12f03cbe-3ac0-3b2d-8c14-12049dfe8b6f",
                                "text": "Unity and democracy are still taking a shellacking here on the home front, despite our successes in the Marshall Islands and in Italy."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "5234b2bc-e323-46c1-8337-270bbdaaf787",
                                "sense_id": "12f03cbe-3ac0-3b2d-8c14-12049dfe8b6f",
                                "text": "After many months of watching its public image take a shellacking as a result of the Jack Abramoff lobbying scandal, Congress finally started to move on lobby reform."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "d11a6f9f-f262-4cbb-8fb0-b318f2b20a01",
                                "sense_id": "12f03cbe-3ac0-3b2d-8c14-12049dfe8b6f",
                                "text": "[C]learly Obama hopes that just as Clinton recovered from his party's midterm shellacking in 1994 to win re-election two years later, so can he."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "82beaf95-a65d-4195-8ac6-7b1e918d7a1f",
                                "sense_id": "12f03cbe-3ac0-3b2d-8c14-12049dfe8b6f",
                                "text": "Bochy was speaking for the masses, who watched a supposed duel of Cy Young award winners evolve into a full-fledged shellacking."
                            },
                            {
                                "example_id": "15a2994c-16b9-4fe8-b5fc-5e6929c583e5",
                                "sense_id": "12f03cbe-3ac0-3b2d-8c14-12049dfe8b6f",
                                "text": "Now, I'm not recommending for every future president that they take a shellacking like I took last night."
                            }
                        ]
                    }
                ],
